<script>
import { url } from '@abide/abide'

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import DealCount from './lib/DealCount.abide'
import dealCount from './lib/DealCount.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import LoadedTotal from './lib/LoadedTotal.abide'
import loadedTotal from './lib/LoadedTotal.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import SameTotal from './lib/SameTotal.abide'
import sameTotal from './lib/SameTotal.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import StageTotal from './lib/StageTotal.abide'
import stageTotal from './lib/StageTotal.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import TabTitle from './lib/TabTitle.abide'
import tabTitle from './lib/TabTitle.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import WinLead from './lib/WinLead.abide'
import winLead from './lib/WinLead.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/reactive/reactive',
        '/reactive/computed',
        '/reactive/memo',
        '/reactive/watch',
        '/reactive/busy',
        '/reactive/ready',
        '/reactive/refresh',
        '/reactive/invalidate',
        '/reactive/tracking',
        '/handlers/get',
        '/orchestration/pipe',
        '/data/fetch-and-handle',
    ]}
>
    <Section title="A read by name subscribes the binding doing the reading">
        <p>Hold the pipeline's deals with <a href={url('/reactive/reactive')}><code>reactive</code></a>
            and read them by name. A read in the template subscribes that one binding, so adding a
            deal runs one binding and leaves the heading beside it alone.</p>
        <Example code={dealCount}><DealCount /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A derived total reruns only when what it read changes">
        <p>A <a href={url('/reactive/computed')}><code>computed</code></a> body subscribes to what it reads,
            the way a template does. Pick a stage and the total reruns, and one binding with it. Type
            a note and nothing the total reads has changed, so no binding runs.</p>
        <Example code={stageTotal}><StageTotal /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A total that comes out the same wakes nothing">
        <p>Renaming a deal changes <code>deals</code>, so the total reruns. It lands on the same
            figure, so nothing that reads the total runs: no binding, no effect.</p>
        <Example code={sameTotal}><SameTotal /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A handler answers a promise, and a computed makes it live">
        <p>Only <a href={url('/reactive/reactive')}><code>reactive</code></a> and
            <a href={url('/reactive/computed')}><code>computed</code></a> are live. A call to a
            handler declared with <a href={url('/handlers/get')}><code>GET</code></a> answers a
            promise, as a <a href={url('/reactive/memo')}><code>memo</code></a>, a
            <a href={url('/orchestration/pipe')}><code>pipe</code></a> and
            <a href={url('/data/fetch-and-handle')}><code>fetchAndHandle</code></a> do, or a
            stream where it yields. Call it inside a <code>computed</code> and the total is live:
            read by name, run again when <code>stage</code> changes, and
            <a href={url('/reactive/ready')}><code>ready()</code></a> says when it first has a
            figure to show.</p>
        <Example code={loadedTotal}><LoadedTotal /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Reload the totals after a write, and keep them on screen">
        <p>A write on the server changes nothing the page holds, so say what it touched. The
            handler's own <a href={url('/reactive/refresh')}><code>refresh</code></a> reloads
            every entry of it while the old figures stay, and each total's
            <a href={url('/reactive/busy')}><code>busy()</code></a> dims them meanwhile. To reload
            on the next read instead, its
            <a href={url('/reactive/invalidate')}><code>invalidate</code></a> marks them stale and
            starts nothing.</p>
        <Example code={winLead}><WinLead /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section title="An effect is the edge where a value leaves the page">
        <p>Everything inside the page is a read. <a href={url('/reactive/watch')}><code>watch</code></a>
            is for what is not: the tab's title, a timer, a call. It reruns when the total
            changes, and its disposer undoes the run before.</p>
        <Example code={tabTitle}><TabTitle /></Example>
    </Section>
</Doc>
